<!--
  ARCHITECTURE.md §1 Wave A, sub-wave A2 — DEPLOY 2 of 2 (create NEW-cased fields + re-add references).

  Recreates the 2 fields at the correct NEW casing (they were destructively deleted in
  DEPLOY 1 / destructiveChangesPost-a2.xml), grants their FLS via the DPEG_Acquisitions
  permission set, and re-points the 3 Apex classes + the FlexiPage spanning fieldInstance
  to the NEW-cased API names.

  New fields:
    - Property_Asset__c.Projected_Value_At_Peak__c  (Currency)
    - Underwriting__c.Cash_On_Cash_Return__c        (Percent)

  FLS: DPEG_Acquisitions carries the readable/editable grants for BOTH fields at the new
  casing (lines 1402 and 1622) — it is the single permission set covering both. (The reader
  maps in agent-output/s1-conformance-requirements.md §9/§10 confirm DPEG_Acquisitions is the
  only permission set granting these two fields.)

  sf orders the dependency graph: CustomFields create first, then Apex compiles against the
  now-existing NEW-cased fields, then the FlexiPage spanning fieldItem resolves.

  Deploy:
    sf project deploy start \
      --manifest manifest/wave-a-case-recase/package-a2-create.xml \
      --target-org DPEG-Acq-5 --test-level RunLocalTests --wait 30
-->
